---
// Component: CredentialPrivacyDiagram
// Visualizes private credentials and revocable space grants
---

<div class="credential-privacy-diagram">
  <div class="privacy-flow">
    <!-- Step 1: Owner -->
    <div class="privacy-flow-node">
      <div class="privacy-node-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M19 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H9a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"/></svg>
      </div>
      <strong>Host</strong>
      <span>Signs in to AI tools on their own computer</span>
    </div>

    <div class="privacy-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>Stays local</span>
      <div class="arrow-line">→</div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 2: Syntila Security Boundary -->
    <div class="privacy-flow-node privacy-flow-node--secure">
      <div class="privacy-node-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
      </div>
      <strong>Host computer</strong>
      <span>Credentials stay with the AI tool here · Not sent to Syntila Cloud or to members' devices</span>
    </div>

    <div class="privacy-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>Requests only</span>
      <div class="arrow-line">→</div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 3: Space Execution -->
    <div class="privacy-flow-node">
      <div class="privacy-node-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
      </div>
      <strong>Space members</strong>
      <span>Send requests to the Space's Workers in shared Threads · Never receive the credentials</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="privacy-grid">
    <div class="privacy-card">
      <span class="privacy-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect width="18" height="11" x="3" y="11" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg>
      </span>
      <strong>Private by default</strong>
      <p>Your API keys, tokens, and provider sign-ins remain on the host computer. Members never see them.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="privacy-card">
      <span class="privacy-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/></svg>
      </span>
      <strong>Chosen per Space</strong>
      <p>You decide which Spaces may use your computer and which Workers each Space gets. Nothing is shared by default.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="privacy-card">
      <span class="privacy-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"/></svg>
      </span>
      <strong>Easy to take back</strong>
      <p>Remove a permission or a member and new requests stop. You do not have to change your provider password or key.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="privacy-card">
      <span class="privacy-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 3v18h18"/><path d="m19 9-5 5-4-4-3 3"/></svg>
      </span>
      <strong>Clear attribution</strong>
      <p>Each run records who asked, which Worker and model answered, and the usage the provider reported.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
